# React and Next.js Frontend

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when the file needs state, effects, browser APIs, refs, GSAP, Three.js, or Next client hooks.
- Keep component props explicitly typed with local `type` aliases. Prefer generated Prismic `Content.*` types and React DOM types over loose objects.
- Use existing primitives such as `Bounded`, `Heading`, `Button`, `ContentBody`, and `PrismicNextLink` before creating new UI building blocks.
- Compose class names with `clsx` when classes are conditional. Let Prettier sort Tailwind classes.
- Keep responsive styling mobile-first with Tailwind variants like `md:` and `lg:`.
- Do not fetch Prismic data in Client Components. Fetch in async Server Components, routes, or helpers, then pass serializable data down.
- Prefer meaningful keys from content fields. Use array indexes only for static separators or content without stable ids.

```tsx
// Good: server component fetches data, child receives typed props.
const client = createClient();
const page = await client.getByUID("page", uid);

return <SomeSection page={page} />;
```
